hapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ\But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, longsuffering, gentleness, goodness, faith,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ3meekness, temperance: against such there is no law.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙRAnd they that are Christ's have crucified the flesh with the affections and lusts.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ9If we live in the Spirit, let us also walk in the Spirit.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙQLet us not be desirous of vain glory, provoking one another, envying one another.¦layout ªlast_verse